th safe free transport could reasonably choose differently.","options":[{"text":"Transport and assignment data first; suggest a free gathering","feedback":"This protects attendance and the deadline while keeping a social option."},{"text":"Outing first, then K80 transport","feedback":"K180 is exhausted and no assignment data is funded."},{"text":"Always remove data because phones are wants","feedback":"Here the data supports a required assignment. Context changes the priority."}],"feedback":{"correctTitle":"Your decision accounts for the constraint","incorrectTitle":"Consider the consequence","correct":"This protects attendance and the deadline while keeping a social option.","low":"K180 is exhausted and no assignment data is funded.","high":"Here the data supports a required assignment. Context changes the priority."}},"checkpoint":[{"id":"lesson-1-2-q1","prompt":"What determines whether data is a need in this scenario?","options":[{"text":"Whether the phone is new","feedback":"The device age does not determine the purpose of this purchase."},{"text":"Whether friends buy it","feedback":"Other people’s choices do not establish this student’s needs."},{"text":"Its role in completing required coursework","feedback":"The purpose and consequences matter."}],"correct":2,"explanation":"The purpose and consequences matter."},{"id":"lesson-1-2-q2","prompt":"K250 is available; essential costs are K190. What remains for other choices?","options":[{"text":"K440","feedback":"Adding costs to funds does not show what remains."},{"text":"K60","feedback":"K250 − K190 = K60."},{"text":"K190","feedback":"That is already committed."}],"correct":1,"explanation":"K250 − K190 = K60."},{"id":"lesson-1-2-q3","prompt":"Buying an outing means giving up needed printing. What is the opportunity cost?","options":[{"text":"The printing that cannot now be purchased","feedback":"It is the alternative given up."},{"text":"The total money ever received","feedback":"Opportunity cost concerns this choice, not all past income."},{"text":"Nothing, because the outing is enjoyable","feedback":"Enjoyable choices still use scarce resources."}],"correct":0,"explanation":"It is the alternative given up."}],"summaryTitle":"Bring the ideas together","takeaways":["Assess needs in context.","Rank consequences and deadlines.","Name what a choice would displace."]}'::jsonb,content='A need supports essential living or an important obligation; a want adds enjoyment or convenience. Context matters: data can be essential for an assignment but discretionary for entertainment. Prioritise the consequence and due date, not the label alone. Opportunity cost is the best alternative you give up when using limited money. Peer pressure can make a purchase feel urgent without changing what it costs. Enjoyment is legitimate, but a plan should make the trade-off visible.',revision=1,estimated_minutes=10,is_published=true where id=lid;
