resources and obligations."},{"text":"Explain the limit and discuss a smaller or non-cash form of help","feedback":"Boundaries can recognise both care and essential needs."},{"text":"Hide the medicine cost to avoid discussion","feedback":"Hiding the constraint makes the trade-off harder to resolve."}],"correct":1,"explanation":"Boundaries can recognise both care and essential needs."}],"summaryTitle":"Bring the ideas together","takeaways":["Check commitments before lending.","Consider who bears the consequences.","Communicate limits respectfully and early."]}'::jsonb,content='An obligation is a payment or responsibility already agreed. A balance can contain money reserved for someone else or for an essential bill. Before lending, ask whose money it is, when it is needed, and what happens if repayment is late. A respectful boundary can explain the commitment and offer a non-financial alternative. Supporting family or friends is a valid priority, but uncertainty and the effects on others should be discussed openly.',revision=1,estimated_minutes=10,is_published=true where id=lid;
