 is still unspent."},{"text":"Reduce recorded transport payments to K200","feedback":"Changing records cannot undo actual expenditure."},{"text":"Spend the delayed support as though received","feedback":"Expected funds are not yet available."}],"feedback":{"correctTitle":"Your decision accounts for the constraint","incorrectTitle":"Consider the consequence","correct":"K60 + K40 = K100 and the source is still unspent.","low":"Changing records cannot undo actual expenditure.","high":"Expected funds are not yet available."}},"checkpoint":[{"id":"lesson-2-4-q1","prompt":"Spending K150 against K120 planned means what?","options":[{"text":"K30 above allocation","feedback":"K150 − K120 = K30 over the plan."},{"text":"K30 still unspent","feedback":"Actual spending already exceeds the plan."},{"text":"K270 available","feedback":"Adding planned and actual figures is not a balance."}],"correct":0,"explanation":"K150 − K120 = K30 over the plan."},{"id":"lesson-2-4-q2","prompt":"A K70 shortfall and K45 unspent optional allocation leave what gap?","options":[{"text":"K115","feedback":"Moving funds reduces the gap rather than adding to it."},{"text":"No gap","feedback":"K45 does not cover K70."},{"text":"K25","feedback":"K70 − K45 = K25 still to address."}],"correct":2,"explanation":"K70 − K45 = K25 still to address."},{"id":"lesson-2-4-q3","prompt":"Essential costs exceed all confirmed resources. What does a useful review do?","options":[{"text":"Hide the largest essential bill","feedback":"Omitting it conceals the unmet need."},{"text":"Identify the gap and explore timing or support without blame","feedback":"A budget reveals constraints; low income is not always solved by cutting."},{"text":"Promise the budget will solve the shortage","feedback":"Planning cannot guarantee more resources."}],"correct":1,"explanation":"A budget reveals constraints; low income is not always solved by cutting."}],"summaryTitle":"Bring the ideas together","takeaways":["Calculate what changed.","Move only funds that remain available.","Make unmet essential needs visible."],"action":{"actionType":"open_budget","destination":"overview","label":"Review My Budget","optional":true}}'::jsonb,content='A variance is the difference between planned and actual or newly forecast spending. State the direction: spending above the plan requires more funding. Review whether a change is temporary or likely to continue. Contingencies reserve room for uncertainty. You can move unspent optional allocations, change timing where safe, or seek support. Do not lower already-spent amounts on paper or remove unavoidable needs just to display a balanced plan.',revision=1,estimated_minutes=10,is_published=true where id=lid;
