K100 is affordable, extend the remaining K900 target to nine months or review the item and costs.","feedback":{"correctTitle":"The calculation is consistent","incorrectTitle":"Recheck the amounts","correct":"(K1,200 − K300) ÷ 6 = K150 each month. If only K100 is affordable, extend the remaining K900 target to nine months or review the item and costs.","low":"Your answer is below the required amount. (K1,200 − K300) ÷ 6 = K150 each month. If only K100 is affordable, extend the remaining K900 target to nine months or review the item and costs.","high":"Your answer is above the required amount. (K1,200 − K300) ÷ 6 = K150 each month. If only K100 is affordable, extend the remaining K900 target to nine months or review the item and costs."}},"checkpoint":[{"id":"lesson-3-2-q1","prompt":"Which goal is most specific?","options":[{"text":"Spend less somehow","feedback":"This does not define a measurable goal."},{"text":"Save K400 for study materials by the start of next term","feedback":"It identifies amount, purpose and deadline."},{"text":"Become rich soon","feedback":"Neither amount nor deadline is clear."}],"correct":1,"explanation":"It identifies amount, purpose and deadline."},{"id":"lesson-3-2-q2","prompt":"A K900 target, K300 already saved and four months require what monthly contribution?","options":[{"text":"K150","feedback":"(K900 − K300) ÷ 4 = K150."},{"text":"K225","feedback":"That ignores existing savings."},{"text":"K600","feedback":"That is the remaining total, not the monthly amount."}],"correct":0,"explanation":"(K900 − K300) ÷ 4 = K150."},{"id":"lesson-3-2-q3","prompt":"The target item increases in price. What should happen?","options":[{"text":"Keep the old target without checking","feedback":"The old total may no longer buy the item."},{"text":"Borrow automatically to preserve the date","feedback":"Borrowing creates a separate affordability decision."},{"text":"Recalculate and compare a revised target or deadline","feedback":"A plan should reflect changed costs and capacity."}],"correct":2,"explanation":"A plan should reflect changed costs and capacity."}],"summaryTitle":"Bring the ideas together","takeaways":["Specify amount, purpose and deadline.","Subtract existing savings first.","Adjust the goal when capacity changes."]}'::jsonb,content='A useful goal names the purpose, target amount and deadline. Subtract existing savings before dividing the remaining target by contribution periods. Compare the result with realistic capacity. If it is too high, consider a later date, a less costly suitable item or a different income plan. Review the goal as prices and circumstances change; a deadline is a planning tool, not a moral test.',revision=1,estimated_minutes=10,is_published=true where id=lid;
