itting funds may help access but can add charges or management difficulty.","options":[{"text":"Reliable short-notice access and security, after checking actual terms","feedback":"These criteria match the purpose; the cheapest-looking option may have access limits."},{"text":"The option with the most enthusiastic recommendation","feedback":"A recommendation does not establish liquidity or security."},{"text":"A payout only in three months because all savings are identical","feedback":"The payout timing does not match an immediate need."}],"feedback":{"correctTitle":"Your decision accounts for the constraint","incorrectTitle":"Consider the consequence","correct":"These criteria match the purpose; the cheapest-looking option may have access limits.","low":"A recommendation does not establish liquidity or security.","high":"The payout timing does not match an immediate need."}},"checkpoint":[{"id":"lesson-3-3-q1","prompt":"What does liquidity describe?","options":[{"text":"Access to money when it is needed","feedback":"Liquidity concerns timely access."},{"text":"How colourful a banking app is","feedback":"Appearance does not determine access."},{"text":"A guarantee of no losses","feedback":"Liquidity and security are separate considerations."}],"correct":0,"explanation":"Liquidity concerns timely access."},{"id":"lesson-3-3-q2","prompt":"An account requires seven days’ notice, but money is needed tomorrow. What is the mismatch?","options":[{"text":"The balance must be zero","feedback":"A positive balance may still be subject to notice."},{"text":"The account must be fraudulent","feedback":"A disclosed notice period is not itself evidence of fraud."},{"text":"The access condition does not fit the deadline","feedback":"The notice period makes the funds unavailable at the needed time."}],"correct":2,"explanation":"The notice period makes the funds unavailable at the needed time."},{"id":"lesson-3-3-q3","prompt":"Before joining a chilimba, what should you clarify?","options":[{"text":"Nothing if a friend participates","feedback":"Trust does not replace understanding the conditions."},{"text":"Contributions, payout order, records and what happens if someone cannot pay","feedback":"These determine obligations and access risks."},{"text":"Only the name of the group","feedback":"A name does not explain the arrangement."}],"correct":1,"explanation":"These determine obligations and access risks."}],"summaryTitle":"Bring the ideas together","takeaways":["Match saving methods to the purpose.","Compare access, security and charges.","Understand informal arrangements before joining."]}'::jsonb,content='Saving methods differ in liquidity, security, accessibility and costs. Cash is immediately usable but can be lost or stolen. Digital access depends on service availability, account security and access points. Bank terms vary; check charges, withdrawal conditions and relevant protections. A chilimba pools contributions under an agreed arrangement; access depends on the payout schedule and members meeting commitments. Trust matters but does not remove default or record-keeping risk. No single option suits every purpose.',revision=1,estimated_minutes=10,is_published=true where id=lid;
