es and obligations","The timing and consequences","Information that still needs verification"]},"concept":{"title":"Understand the decision","introduction":"A loan provides money now in exchange for repayment under agreed terms. A gift has no repayment obligation if that is clearly agreed. Principal is the amount borrowed; repayment may include additional costs. Formal and informal borrowing can both create obligations. With friends or family, clarify whether support is a gift or a loan to avoid conflict. Informal moneylending, sometimes called kaloba, can involve difficult costs or collection practices; do not assume its terms or protections match a regulated lender.","takeaway":"Clarify gift versus loan.","definitions":[{"term":"Principal","meaning":"The original amount borrowed.","detail":"Apply this distinction to the situation and worked example before choosing your response."},{"term":"Repayment obligation","meaning":"The amount and timing you agree to repay.","detail":"Apply this distinction to the situation and worked example before choosing your response."}]},"example":{"title":"Work through the situation","introduction":"Follow the reasoning. These figures illustrate the decision; they are not current prices, fees or product recommendations.","income":0,"rows":[],"steps":["Accepting a K100 gift and K100 loan provides K200 now.","Only the K100 loan is repayable under the stated agreement; check whether any charge applies.","The K200 informal offer cannot be compared until total repayment, due date and consequences are clear."],"showBudgetTable":false},"practice":{"kind":"choice","prompt":"What should Peter establish before accepting support?","context":"Use the information in the situation. Choose a response, then examine its consequences.","correct":0,"unit":"","hint":"Clarify gift versus loan.","consequence":"The K200 informal offer cannot be compared until total repayment, due date and consequences are clear.","options":[{"text":"Whether it is a gift or loan, the total due and repayment date","feedback":"Clear terms reveal obligations and reduce misunderstandings."},{"text":"Only how quickly he can receive it","feedback":"Speed does not reveal cost or repayment risk."},{"text":"Assume all money from friends is a gift","feedback":"A friend can expect repayment; ask explicitly."}],"feedback":{"correctTitle":"Your decision accounts for the constraint","incorrectTitle":"Consider the consequence","correct":"Clear terms reveal obligations and reduce misunderstandings.","low":"Speed does not reveal cost or repayment risk.","high":"A friend can expect repayment; ask explicitly."}},"checkpoint":[{"id":"lesson-4-1-q1","prompt":"Which statement describes a loan?","options":[{"text":"Any income earned through work","feedback":"Earnings are not automatically repayable."},{"text":"Money provided with an obligation to repay","feedback":"Repayment distinguishes a loan from a clearly agreed gift."},{"text":"Money that is always free","feedback":"Loans may involve interest or charges."}],"correct":1,"explanation":"Repayment distinguishes a loan from a clearly agreed gift."},{"id":"lesson-4-1-q2","prompt":"K300 is borrowed and K340 must be repaid. What is the principal?","options":[{"text":"K300","feedback":"Principal is the original borrowed amount."},{"text":"K40","feedback":"K40 is the additional cost in this example."},{"text":"K340","feedback":"K340 is total repayment."}],"correct":0,"explanation":"Principal is the original borrowed amount."},{"id":"lesson-4-1-q3","prompt":"A lender will not explain repayment terms. What is prudent?","options":[{"text":"Sign because the amount is small","feedback":"Small loans can still carry harmful conditions."},{"text":"Assume informal means interest-free","feedback":"Informal arrangements can carry charges."},{"text":"Pause until the obligations are clear and compare alternatives","feedback":"Unknown obligations prevent an informed affordability decision."}],"correct":2,"explanation":"Unknown obligations prevent an informed affordability decision."}],"summaryTitle":"Bring the ideas together","takeaways":["Clarify gift versus loan.","Know amount, timing and conditions.","Do not accept unclear obligations."]}'::jsonb,content='A loan provides money now in exchange for repayment under agreed terms. A gift has no repayment obligation if that is clearly agreed. Principal is the amount borrowed; repayment may include additional costs. Formal and informal borrowing can both create obligations. With friends or family, clarify whether support is a gift or a loan to avoid conflict. Informal moneylending, sometimes called kaloba, can involve difficult costs or collection practices; do not assume its terms or protections match a regulated lender.',revision=1,estimated_minutes=10,is_published=true where id=lid;
