se an unwanted action."},{"text":"Refund the screenshot amount immediately","feedback":"A screenshot does not prove receipt and the requested destination may differ."}],"feedback":{"correctTitle":"Your decision accounts for the constraint","incorrectTitle":"Consider the consequence","correct":"This protects credentials while checking whether any real transaction occurred.","low":"The code may authorise an unwanted action.","high":"A screenshot does not prove receipt and the requested destination may differ."}},"checkpoint":[{"id":"lesson-5-3-q1","prompt":"Which is a warning sign?","options":[{"text":"Keeping a receipt privately","feedback":"Private records can help resolve issues."},{"text":"Pressure to reveal an OTP immediately","feedback":"Urgency and credential requests are common manipulation tactics."},{"text":"Checking your own statement","feedback":"That is an independent verification step."}],"correct":1,"explanation":"Urgency and credential requests are common manipulation tactics."},{"id":"lesson-5-3-q2","prompt":"You disclosed a PIN to a suspicious caller. What should you do?","options":[{"text":"Use official provider channels promptly to secure the account and report it","feedback":"Acting quickly may limit further access; follow verified provider instructions."},{"text":"Wait until the caller confirms they are finished","feedback":"That prolongs exposure."},{"text":"Post the PIN publicly to warn others","feedback":"That exposes it to more people."}],"correct":0,"explanation":"Acting quickly may limit further access; follow verified provider instructions."},{"id":"lesson-5-3-q3","prompt":"Why avoid a support number inside a suspicious message?","options":[{"text":"All support services are fraudulent","feedback":"Legitimate support exists; verify the channel."},{"text":"A local number guarantees safety","feedback":"A local number alone does not establish identity."},{"text":"It may lead back to the attacker","feedback":"Independent contact details avoid trusting the same unverified source."}],"correct":2,"explanation":"Independent contact details avoid trusting the same unverified source."}],"summaryTitle":"Bring the ideas together","takeaways":["Keep PINs and OTPs private.","Verify through independent channels.","Preserve evidence and report suspected compromise."]}'::jsonb,content='Social engineering pressures people into revealing information or moving money. Phishing uses deceptive messages or sites to obtain credentials. PINs and one-time passwords authorise access or actions and should not be shared with callers. Screenshots and sender names can be falsified. Verify through your own app or independently obtained provider contact. If a genuine mistaken transfer appears, use the provider’s official resolution process rather than improvising a payment to a stranger. Report suspected compromise promptly.',revision=1,estimated_minutes=10,is_published=true where id=lid;
